# Laravel Security Rules

- Validate and authorize every request.
- Use parameterized queries/Eloquent bindings; never build unsafe SQL from raw user input.
- Protect against mass assignment with guarded/fillable strategy appropriate to the model.
- Rate-limit authentication, negotiation, sync, and other abuse-prone endpoints.
- Sanitize/validate uploaded files and control storage access.
- Encrypt or otherwise protect sensitive data where required by policy.
- Never commit secrets, API keys, credentials, private certificates, or production tokens.
- Logs MUST be structured and must exclude secrets and unnecessary sensitive personal data.
- Keep audit logs for privileged actions and critical business state changes.
- Apply least privilege to service accounts and external integrations.
- Respect documented LGPD data minimization, retention, access, correction, and deletion rules.
